This composition looks like a precipitation-hardened maraging stainless steel, similar to PH 13-8Mo or Custom 455. It has Cr 10–12, Ni 10, Mo about 2, and Ti and Al additions. Ni, Ti and Al form NiAl and Ni3Ti precipitates. Aged steels of this type typically reach about 1500–1700 MPa. Since this is an estimate from memory, I did not run a search.

I chose a value near the middle of that range.

